# Kingfisher GNSS discipline example.
# Merge into /etc/chrony/chrony.conf (Debian / Raspberry Pi OS).
#
# Boot policy: step (not just slew) when offset exceeds 0.5 s, with no limit on
# how many times at boot. Required for automatic PPS lock on RTC-backed Pi boot:
# GPS serial and PPS can disagree by ~600 ms until chrony steps; makestep 1.0 3
# never fires and both sources stay #x ("no majority").
makestep 0.5 -1
rtcsync

# Offline-first flight recording: leave pool commented out.
#pool pool.ntp.org iburst

# gpsd serial-time SOCK for /dev/ttyAMA0.
# Recent gpsd uses chrony.clk.<device>.sock for serial time and chrony.<pps>.sock
# for PPS time.
#
# offset 0.62: pipeline delay between PPS edge and gpsd serial time-of-day on the
# M9N (independent of RTC battery). Tune once via NTP cross-check at offset 0.0
# if receiver or gpsd version changes — see docs/time-sync.md.
#
# poll/filter: default refclock poll is 4 (16 s/sample), which makes GPS take
# minutes to become selectable and PPS (lock GPS) even longer at boot. poll 2
# (4 s) + filter 3 lets GPS converge and PPS lock within ~1 min of 3D fix.
refclock SOCK /run/chrony.clk.ttyAMA0.sock refid GPS precision 1e-1 offset 0.62 delay 0.1 poll 2 filter 3

# PPS follow-on (GPIO 18 -> /dev/pps0, also in gpsd DEVICES). Use SOCK PPS —
# do not also enable refclock PPS /dev/pps0; gpsd holds the device.
# Keep PPS poll == GPS poll so lock GPS always has a recent time-of-day sample.
refclock SOCK /run/chrony.pps0.sock refid PPS precision 1e-7 lock GPS poll 2

# --- Alternative profiles (pick one set of refclock lines) ---
#
# UART-only (no PPS in chrony): simpler auto-boot with RTC battery; ~ms accuracy.
# Use offset 0.0 when the Pi RTC keeps coarse time at boot (not +620 ms).
# refclock SOCK /run/chrony.clk.ttyAMA0.sock refid GPS precision 1e-1 offset 0.0 delay 0.1 poll 2 filter 3
#
# PPS-only (no GPS refclock): sub-us accuracy; gpsd still needs GPS fix so PPS
# SOCK carries absolute UTC seconds. RTC + makestep 0.5 -1 provide coarse boot time.
# refclock SOCK /run/chrony.pps0.sock refid PPS precision 1e-7 poll 2
